<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niccolò Piccinino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1386–1444</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niccolò Piccinino was an Italian condottiere from Perugia, a pupil of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/braccio-da-montone">Braccio da Montone</a>, who led the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/filippo-maria-visconti">Filippo Maria Visconti</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, from the 1420s to the 1440s. He fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">Papacy</a> and was defeated by the Florentines and papal forces at the Battle of Anghiari in 1440. He died in Milan in 1444.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niccolo-piccinino.jpg" alt="Niccolò Piccinino" width="320" height="491" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pisanello · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pisanello_-_Codex_Vallardi_2482.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
